      "text": "To solve the expression \\(8 + 6(3-8)^2\\), we will follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\n1. **Evaluate the expression inside the parentheses:**\n   \\[\n   3 - 8 = -5\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   8 + 6(-5)^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Evaluate the exponent:**\n   \\[\n   (-5)^2 = 25\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   8 + 6 \\times 25\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 25 = 150\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   8 + 150\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the addition:**\n   \\[\n   8 + 150 = 158\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{158}\n\\]",
